{"id": "EUVD-2026-97041", "enisaUuid": "c12ab8b5-1c15-3f80-b6c7-85ed0d69b911", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SystemApiController getUserRoleSetById handler that allows any authenticated user to read other users' role assignments. Low-privileged attackers can supply an arbitrary userId parameter to retrieve assigned role codes and identify administrator accounts without the system:user:queryUserRole permission.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:59:21", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_api_user_role_set_by_id.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L440-L443", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-getuserrolesetbyid"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108867", "GHSA-h752-2r87-c7w9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "62531f52-0317-3c75-95f6-3b7105da918c", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "65160150-3e30-374f-a188-2798afc22923", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}